In `maybe_promote`, `dtype_` and `fill_value` are assigned in each branch of the `if`/`elif` chain, then both flow into the common tail: `dtype_` is used at `dtype_out = np.dtype(dtype_)`, and `fill_value` is used at `fill_value = dtype_out.type(fill_value)` and then returned. The test calls `maybe_promote` with five dtypes: float64, int64, complex128, datetime64[ns], and object. Those inputs take the real-floating, integral, complex-floating, datetime64, and final `else` branches respectively, so the covered defs are the assignments in those branches plus the redefinition of `fill_value` at the cast line before the return.

